1
00:00:00,410 --> 00:00:04,040
(Penny:)How are we supposed to set up machines
and conveyor belts in my apartment?

2
00:00:04,205 --> 00:00:06,375
(Sheldon:)You're thinking of
the moving assembly line.

3
00:00:06,541 --> 00:00:10,041
(Sheldon:)An understandable,
but not excusable, mistake. Now...

4
00:00:10,962 --> 00:00:14,212
(Sheldon:)...the moving assembly line, that was
introduced by Henry Ford in 1908.

5
00:00:14,382 --> 00:00:17,762
(Sheldon:)That innovation is what made possible
our modern consumer culture...

6
00:00:17,927 --> 00:00:20,387
...by enabling a low unit cost
for manufactured goods.

7
00:00:20,555 --> 00:00:24,895
(Sheldon:)I guess that isn't one of the topics
discussed on your Radiohead.

8
00:00:28,688 --> 00:00:30,438
We're gonna miss the coming attractions.

9
00:00:30,606 --> 00:00:31,646
[GROANS]

10
00:00:31,816 --> 00:00:33,396
(Raj:)What's the matter?

11
00:00:36,946 --> 00:00:40,616
(Howard:)I think I bruised a testicle
capturing that last pawn.

12
00:00:42,285 --> 00:00:47,125
[PENNY & SHELDON SINGING
"BLOW THE MAN DOWN"]

13
00:00:47,290 --> 00:00:50,790
PENNY & SHELDON [SINGING]:
Give me some time to blow the man down

14
00:00:50,960 --> 00:00:53,840
I'm a deep-water sailor
Just come from Hong Kong

15
00:00:54,005 --> 00:00:56,925
BOTH:
To me way, hey, blow the man down

16
00:00:57,091 --> 00:01:00,131
If you give me some whiskey
I'll sing you a song

